WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.150 --> 00:00:03.200
Every screen on your boat needs electricity.

2
00:00:03.450 --> 00:00:08.625
One instrument doesn’t, and it’s the one that will get you home when the rest go dark.

3
00:00:08.875 --> 00:00:10.875
The magnetic compass.

4
00:00:11.125 --> 00:00:12.700
It’s simple.

5
00:00:12.950 --> 00:00:19.000
A magnetized card floats in liquid, and it lines itself up with the earth’s magnetic field.

6
00:00:19.250 --> 00:00:21.125
The card stays still.

7
00:00:21.375 --> 00:00:23.275
The boat turns around it.

8
00:00:23.525 --> 00:00:28.025
The lubber line is a mark on the bowl, lined up with the boat’s centerline.

9
00:00:28.275 --> 00:00:31.925
Your heading is the number on the card at the lubber line.

10
00:00:32.175 --> 00:00:38.350
So the compass must be mounted on the centerline, or parallel to it, where the helmsman can see it.

11
00:00:38.600 --> 00:00:42.150
Keep magnetic and electrical things away from it.

12
00:00:42.400 --> 00:00:45.200
Speakers, radios, phones, tools.

13
00:00:45.450 --> 00:00:48.100
Even a cup holder with a magnet in it.

14
00:00:48.350 --> 00:00:50.625
Why does that matter so much?

15
00:00:51.625 --> 00:00:57.025
Because moving any of them changes the compass’s error, and you won’t know by how much.

16
00:00:57.275 --> 00:01:00.725
And the gimbals keep the card level as the boat rolls.
